[Applause]  e.t can confirm american idol winner  lane hardy has been arrested for  allegedly planting a listening device in  a female student's dorm room at  louisiana state university  according to booking documents obtained  by et on friday the country crooner is  charged with leaving a listening device  in his ex-girlfriend's room in order to  monitor her conversations when they  broke up  the two reportedly dated from november  2021 to february 2022 and according to  the docs she found the device which at  first appeared to be a phone charger  under her futon and later learned it was  a voice-activated recorder e.t has  reached out to hardy's reps for comment  but on thursday the 21 year old singer  shared his own statement on facebook  acknowledging that the lsu pd issued a  warrant for his arrest due to  allegations made against him and while  the ai alum didn't say what he was being  accused of he did note that he was fully  cooperative with cops adding that he  understands his career thrust him into  the public spotlight something he says  he embraces wholeheartedly however due  to the sensitive nature of this  allegation i humbly ask for privacy at  this time i have the utmost respect for  the law and will assist in their  investigation as needed moving forward  according to the docs hardy allegedly  had information about the victim and her  actions during christmas break that was  not known to the defendant  and when the female student confronted  hardy he allegedly admitted that he left  a bug in her room but later discarded it  in his pond  [Music]  the singer won season 17 of american  idol back in 2019.  my mind is so overwhelmed right now with  so many different emotions  and i really need to  let it sink in it hasn't sinked in yet  i'm still processing it but it's been a  crazy ride and it's been a lot of  tough situations and a lot of mental  stress and stuff and  it feels i feel it feels great and e.t  was with hardy earlier this month at the  great idol reunion where he opened up  about returning for the show's 20-year  anniversary celebration this is a huge  milestone for american idol and like  being part of their 20th year  anniversary is going to go down the  history of this show so it's pretty cool  to be part of it best piece of advice  for people coming on to american idol  trust your gut and stay open-minded  [Music]

